6. Full Replication Specification
6.1 Replication Schema
The replication schema defines the structure of a replication deposit.

It has the following fields:

replication_id. A string. Required.

original_claim_id. A string. Required.

original_paper_reference. A string. Required.

replication_paper_reference. A string. Required.

field. A string. Required.

subfield. A string. Optional.

replication_method. An object. It contains design, sample_size, instruments, statistical_pipeline, and preregistration_status.

replication_outcome. An enum. The values are success, failure, partial, inconclusive.

effect_size_original. A number. Optional.

effect_size_replication. A number. Optional.

effect_size_confidence_interval_original. An object. Optional.

effect_size_confidence_interval_replication. An object. Optional.

difference_reason. A string. Optional.

difference_category. An enum. The values are sampling_error, measurement_error, selection_effect, analysis_choice, population_difference, contextual_difference, unknown, other.

replication_date. A string in ISO8601 format. Required.

replicator_id. A string. Required.

replicator_affiliation. A string. Optional.

provenance. An object. It contains source, tool_version, and notes.

stag_annotation. An object. Optional.

null_model_result. An object. Optional.

numerical_verification_result. An object. Optional.

keywords. An array of strings. Optional.

notes. A string. Optional.

moderation_status. An enum. The values are pending, approved, rejected. The default is pending.

version. An integer. The default is 1.

supersedes. A string. Optional.

superseded_by. A string. Optional.

