6.3 Referential Integrity
The database enforces the following constraints.

Every stag_link.replication_id must exist in replication.

Every null_model_link.replication_id must exist in replication.

Every verification_link.replication_id must exist in replication.

Every provenance.replication_id must exist in replication.

Every moderation.replication_id must exist in replication.

The version chain (supersedes and superseded_by) must be acyclic.

Every original_claim_id must resolve to a claim in the Physics Knowledge Library, or be flagged as unresolved.

