7. Core Logic as Executable Pseudocode
7.1 Create Replication
function createReplication(replication, files, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "replicator"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. validationResult = validateReplication(replication). If invalid, return an error with the details.

Step 3. originalClaim = lookupClaim(replication.original_claim_id). If null, set replication.original_claim_id_unresolved to true.

Step 4. If replication.stag_annotation is not null, validate it against the STAG schema.

Step 5. If replication.null_model_result is not null, validate it against the Null-Model Protocol schema.

Step 6. replicationId = generateReplicationId(). Set the fields: replication_id, version 1, moderation_status pending, replication_date now, replicator_id from auth, replicator_affiliation from auth, provenance from provenance.

Step 7. insertReplication(replication).

Step 8. If replication.stag_annotation is not null, insertSTAGLink.

Step 9. If replication.null_model_result is not null, insertNullModelLink.

Step 10. If replication.numerical_verification_result is not null, insertVerificationLink.

Step 11. insertProvenance.

Step 12. insertModeration with status pending.

Step 13. insertAuditLog.

Step 14. return the replication_id and the status created.

7.2 Read Replication
function readReplication(replicationId, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. replication = selectReplication(replicationId). If null, return an error.

Step 3. Read the links, the provenance, the moderation, and the original claim.

Step 4. Reconstruct the deposit.

Step 5. insertAuditLog.

Step 6. return the deposit.

7.3 Update Replication
function updateReplication(replicationId, replication, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "replicator"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. existing = selectReplication(replicationId). If null, return an error.

Step 3. Validate the new replication.

Step 4. newVersion = existing.version + 1. Update the version, supersedes, and superseded_by fields.

Step 5. insertProvenance with operation update.

Step 6. insertAuditLog.

Step 7. return the replication_id, the version, and the status updated.

7.4 Delete Replication
function deleteReplication(replicationId, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "admin"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. existing = selectReplication(replicationId). If null, return an error.

Step 3. If soft delete, mark as deleted. Otherwise, remove the record.

Step 4. insertAuditLog.

Step 5. return the replication_id and the status deleted.

