12. Validation Engine Design
The tracker validates the following.

Validation 1. Replication validity. Every replication attempt is validated against the replication schema before it is stored.

Validation 2. STAG annotation validity. Every STAG annotation is validated against the STAG schema and the thirty-two semantic rules.

Validation 3. Null-Model Protocol result validity. Every Null-Model Protocol result is validated against the Null-Model Protocol schema.

Validation 4. Numerical verification result validity. Every numerical verification result is validated against the verification schema.

Validation 5. Referential integrity. Every foreign key reference must resolve to an existing record.

Validation 6. Version chain acyclicity. The version chain must be acyclic.

Validation 7. Original claim resolution. Every original_claim_id must resolve to a claim in the Physics Knowledge Library, or be flagged as unresolved.

Validation 8. Provenance completeness. Every replication attempt must have a provenance record.

Validation 9. Audit completeness. Every operation must have an audit log entry.

Validation 10. Moderation completeness. Every replication attempt must have a moderation record.

Validation 11. Effect-size consistency. If both effect sizes are recorded, the difference must be consistent with the recorded values.

